            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your patient, a 73-year-old female, admitted on 14th September 2019 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry were performed to assess severity. Blood tests confirmed an inflammatory response. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. Clinical response was satisfactory, with improvement in respiratory function and oxygenation. She was discharged on 15th September 2019 in stable condition with an optimised inhaler regimen and a short course of oral steroids. I recommend close follow-up and reinforcement of her COPD management plan. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
